    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24">

                <pb facs="0167" n="49" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg49"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867n.404Wailing Wall/27: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-26T21:00:00+02:00">August 26, 1929—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:54 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>British authorities sent armed convoy Hebron today to evacuate Jewish
                    noncombatants guarded in Hebron police barracks. British authorities promised to
                    evacuate Americans and I sent Simon, Jewish <pb facs="0168" n="50" xml:id="pg50"
                    /> member of the consulate general, with a convoy to obtain list of names of all
                    American citizens, including dead and wounded, and to assist evacuation of the
                    living. All Americans are now evacuated except 14 students and 2 others who
                    refused to leave without the other students, but it is hoped to secure their
                    evacuation tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
